;; Scratch probe (arc 255, three-orphans stone) — original question, for HashMap: does
;; eval_hashmap_ctor's is_type_arg_shaped guard (Keyword|List only) reject a
;; well-typed `[T :-> R]` fn-type-bracket K/V that check-time (parse_type_node,
;; via parse_param_spec_slot) accepts?
;;
;; .wat.bad (Stone 255.74): that question is now MOOT — a fn-typed HashMap key is a key-eligible
;; wall violation (`is_atomizable`), so the checker refuses this before `eval_hashmap_ctor` is
;; ever reached. Was a bare `.wat` (type-checked clean) until this stone wired `is_atomizable`
;; into `infer_hashmap_constructor`; renamed `.wat` -> `.wat.bad` to match (floor:
;; `wat_scripts_fixes_load::every_wat_scripts_file_loads_on_the_current_runtime` caught it as
;; newly-rotted). See `wat-scripts/probes/arc-255/probe-255.74-a-key-must-be-data.wat.bad` for
;; the recorded fixture (the HashSet sibling of this exact shape).
(:wat::core::def :user::main
  (:wat::core::fn [] -> wat.type/nil
    (:wat::kernel::println
      (wat.type/HashMap :- [[wat.type/i64 :-> wat.type/bool] wat.type/i64]))))
